Whittaker fits generalized additive models in Python: regressions where each effect is a smooth
curve shaped by the data, with **how smooth chosen for you**. It brings the depth of R's mgcv to
Pandas, Polars, and any [Narwhals](https://narwhals-dev.github.io/narwhals/) frame, with an
interactive chart for every fit.

